{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Grace, thanks for reaching out. I've put in a request to reset your Brightline password, and a technician needs to approve it. We can't set the password you suggested. 12345678 is too easy to guess and doesn't meet our security rules. Once the reset is approved, a technician will phone you at the number we have on file with a temporary password. You'll be asked to pick a new one the first time you sign in. Please choose something long and unique that you don't use anywhere else. Also, you aren't set up with Duo yet. Setting it up would let you reset your own password next time without waiting on us. Just let us know if you'd like help with that.",
  "internal_note": "Request came from the sender's own verified email (user_id 11, Grace Okafor, Receptionist, not VIP). Account is active with 0 failed logins and no lockout, so no unlock is needed. Not enrolled in Duo, so self-service reset isn't available. Queued reset_password (approval id 1). Per policy this sets a system temporary password that must be changed at next sign-in. The user's requested password '12345678' must NOT be used. Please deliver the temporary password by phone to the number on file. Suggest following up on Duo enrollment.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-002"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
